./SHEET6-DIRECTIONB.md:2049:> ## 3. The exact D25 discrimination logic
./SHEET6-DIRECTIONB.md:2059:> ### 3.1 D25 EMPTY
./SHEET6-DIRECTIONB.md:2069:> > **THEOREM AT THE STATED SCOPE:** family-wide D25 EMPTY proves that every D23 survivor was a finite-depth mirage and that no mod $p$ formal germ exists on the residue-A, B-frozen, no-log, `PIN42`, $W_1W_2\ne0$ chart at that prime and the atlas's fixed $r_3$ embedding.
./SHEET6-DIRECTIONB.md:2073:> D25 EMPTY is the point at which the residue-A kill campaign **resumes**, not the point at which a characteristic-zero theorem may already be announced. Repeat the exhaustive family calculation at a second good prime, then seek an exact $\mathbf Q(\sqrt3)$ identity with source-row provenance and discharge the conjugate $r_3$ embedding, other charts, no-log/`PIN42` coverage, and B-unfreezing. Modular emptiness alone is a screening-tier result.
./SHEET6-DIRECTIONB.md:2075:> ### 3.2 D25 NONEMPTY
./SHEET6-DIRECTIONB.md:2077:> D25 NONEMPTY proves only that at least one point of $V_{25}$ projects to the D23 survivor locus. It deepens finite-window survival; it does not produce an inverse-limit point, a formal germ, a characteristic-zero germ, an algebraic branch, or a polynomial Keller pair.
./SHEET6-DIRECTIONB.md:2087:> ### 3.3 The corrected $e$-test at D25
./SHEET6-DIRECTIONB.md:2089:> The D25 threshold is
./SHEET6-DIRECTIONB.md:2095:> Recompute the exact low-band part of $L_s^+$ at genuine reconstructed D25 points using the true deep labels. A finite D25 point does **not** determine its $t^{42+}$ x-side completion. Before following $H_{29}$ beyond its first coefficient, do one of three things: use a sufficiently long explicitly compatible lift that supplies every coefficient consumed; prove a finite-range invariance lemma; or retain and quantify over the unspecified completion variables. Never silently zero-fill them.
./SHEET6-DIRECTIONB.md:2105:> | corrected D25 behavior | exact conclusion |
./SHEET6-DIRECTIONB.md:2109:> | Finite promoted $e^+(s)>12$ | D25 is too shallow; target $D=2e^+(s)+1$. |
./SHEET6-DIRECTIONB.md:2110:> | Certified \(\ell^+(s)>12\) | This point cannot supply a D25 Hensel certificate; it may still extend singularly. |
./SHEET6-DIRECTIONB.md:2116:> A locus-wide claim that no D25 point has $e^+\le12$ requires symbolic stratification of every D25 component. Witness sampling cannot prove it. If the present \(\ell^+\ge31\) obstruction persists at a D25 point, then any finite-$e$ target for that point is at least D63; this is not itself evidence of nonextension.
