./dist/jc72108-theory-bundle-v1/xmodel/grok-h5a-review.md:20:  **Printed Notation 3.5 is P-ambiguous.** Verbatim p.12: “Assume \(F=I_P(u)\) for some \(P\) … Set \(\kappa_F:=\kappa/e_j\), where \(\alpha_j\le u<\alpha_{j+1}\).” Two presentations of the same vertex can (and in case III do) give two values. The lattice identities (1) are the definitions: adjoining \(P\)’s jump at \(v\) multiplies the common index \(L_0\) by \(\nu_G\), so \(\kappa_G=\nu_G L_0\); \(Q\)’s jump at \(u\) multiplies it by \(\nu_F\), so \(\kappa_F(Q)=\nu_F L_0\).
