./xmodel/sol-round6.md:327:## 3. The exact D25 discrimination logic
./xmodel/sol-round6.md:337:### 3.1 D25 EMPTY
./xmodel/sol-round6.md:347:> **THEOREM AT THE STATED SCOPE:** family-wide D25 EMPTY proves that every D23 survivor was a finite-depth mirage and that no mod $p$ formal germ exists on the residue-A, B-frozen, no-log, `PIN42`, $W_1W_2\ne0$ chart at that prime and the atlas's fixed $r_3$ embedding.
./xmodel/sol-round6.md:351:D25 EMPTY is the point at which the residue-A kill campaign **resumes**, not the point at which a characteristic-zero theorem may already be announced. Repeat the exhaustive family calculation at a second good prime, then seek an exact $\mathbf Q(\sqrt3)$ identity with source-row provenance and discharge the conjugate $r_3$ embedding, other charts, no-log/`PIN42` coverage, and B-unfreezing. Modular emptiness alone is a screening-tier result.
./xmodel/sol-round6.md:353:### 3.2 D25 NONEMPTY
./xmodel/sol-round6.md:355:D25 NONEMPTY proves only that at least one point of $V_{25}$ projects to the D23 survivor locus. It deepens finite-window survival; it does not produce an inverse-limit point, a formal germ, a characteristic-zero germ, an algebraic branch, or a polynomial Keller pair.
./xmodel/sol-round6.md:365:### 3.3 The corrected $e$-test at D25
./xmodel/sol-round6.md:367:The D25 threshold is
./xmodel/sol-round6.md:373:Recompute the exact low-band part of $L_s^+$ at genuine reconstructed D25 points using the true deep labels. A finite D25 point does **not** determine its $t^{42+}$ x-side completion. Before following $H_{29}$ beyond its first coefficient, do one of three things: use a sufficiently long explicitly compatible lift that supplies every coefficient consumed; prove a finite-range invariance lemma; or retain and quantify over the unspecified completion variables. Never silently zero-fill them.
./xmodel/sol-round6.md:383:| corrected D25 behavior | exact conclusion |
./xmodel/sol-round6.md:387:| Finite promoted $e^+(s)>12$ | D25 is too shallow; target $D=2e^+(s)+1$. |
./xmodel/sol-round6.md:388:| Certified \(\ell^+(s)>12\) | This point cannot supply a D25 Hensel certificate; it may still extend singularly. |
./xmodel/sol-round6.md:394:A locus-wide claim that no D25 point has $e^+\le12$ requires symbolic stratification of every D25 component. Witness sampling cannot prove it. If the present \(\ell^+\ge31\) obstruction persists at a D25 point, then any finite-$e$ target for that point is at least D63; this is not itself evidence of nonextension.
./xmodel/sol-round6.md:398:These are subjective epistemic estimates, not certificate grades. The 6/22/72 fiber-outcome partition is conditional on the exact family object and a completed modular verdict; it describes the mathematical outcome, not the probability that the compiler finishes. The small-candidate and loss rows are additionally conditional on D25 NONEMPTY and witness extraction. The outcomes are correlated; the 36 components must not be modeled as independent trials.
./xmodel/sol-round6.md:403:| All 36 D25 fibers EMPTY | **6%** (5--10%) | D23 leaves an 11-dimensional locus on every fiber and Row 24 contributes at most five existential residuals; a kill needs a structured unit ideal, not an equation count. |
./xmodel/sol-round6.md:404:| Mixed EMPTY/NONEMPTY D25 mask | **22%** (15--30%) | Coefficients genuinely vary and the combined class key distinguishes all fibers, despite shared support. |
./xmodel/sol-round6.md:405:| All 36 D25 fibers NONEMPTY | **72%** (60--80%) | Family-wide codimension-two survival and common support make continued correlated survival the modal outcome. |
./xmodel/sol-round6.md:406:| At least one D25 survivor | **94%** | Complement of family-wide EMPTY. |
./xmodel/sol-round6.md:407:| Corrected `E_CANDIDATE^+ <= 12` somewhere | **5%** (3--10%) | Every corrected D23 sample already has \(\ell^+\ge31\); this extrapolates from 36 `a00pp` operators, not from all atlas fibers, and D25 may select a better-conditioned sublocus. |
./xmodel/sol-round6.md:408:| Initial D25 samples still have corrected loss (>12) | **90%** (85--95%) | The same \(\ell^+\ge31\) finite-window obstruction is uniform across all sampled points and both tested primes on `a00pp`; the all-depth loss itself is undetermined. |
./xmodel/sol-round6.md:409:| Fully promoted D25 formal-germ certificate in this round | **2%** (1--4%) | A small value would still need CYCLIC-30, an Ore parametrix, the completed-ideal bridge, and E-HENSEL. |
./xmodel/sol-round6.md:411:**CONJECTURE / LOW CONFIDENCE.** Conditional on D25 NONEMPTY but no candidate at or below 12, I currently split the route-wide outcomes approximately 60% that every D25 survivor dies at some later finite depth versus 40% that at least one scoped mod $p$ formal germ exists, with uncertainty of at least 20 percentage points in either direction. The latter germ could have finite (e^+>12) and simply be too deep for D25 certification; it need not be infinitely singular. Stabilized finite $e^+$ would move probability sharply toward germ-track; continued growth of \(\delta^+\), \(\ell^+\), and projection codimension would move it toward mirage. The probability that this local modular route already yields a polynomial characteristic-zero counterexample remains below 1%.
