./dist/jc72108-theory-bundle-v1/xmodel/sol-h5a.md:122:The thesis provides an independent in-context check in Proposition 5.5 (printed pp. 26--27). In its \(c=0\) case, \(P\) is explicitly the nonjump presentation, with Puiseux characteristics \((\kappa,\beta_1,\ldots,\beta_m)\) and \(\alpha_m<u\). It then says that any other \(Q\) realizing \(F\) has ramification index \(\nu_F\kappa\), preserves the earlier characteristic exponents, and appends \(u\) as the new characteristic exponent. The tuple as printed is dimensionally garbled—it leaves the old integer numerator indices unscaled and writes rational \(u\) in an integer slot—but its ramification factor and the following displayed ratio are unambiguous.
