+Consequently the precise relationship is
+
+\[
+ \boxed{
+ \nu_{P_i}\mid\kappa_i,
+ \qquad
+ \kappa_i
+ =\nu_{P_i}\!!
+  \prod_{\substack{F<P_i\\F\ \mathrm{characteristic}}}\!\nu_F.} \tag{1.6}
+\]
+
+It is **not**
+\(\kappa_i=\prod_{P\text{ lying on the branch}}\nu_P\): the latter
+product has the single factor \(\nu_{P_i}\).
